course: dictionary
lesson: 136
title: Advertising
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Advertising is the business of making adverts. An advert tells people about a product or service and tries to persuade them to buy it. When you see the word, look at the words around it. «Own-brand food is often made in a similar way to famous brands but costs less because there is no big advertising.» The clue is costs less: the famous brands spend lots of money on adverts, and the own-brand food does not.
explain: Advertising can also be the -ing form of «advertise», which means telling people about something publicly, in adverts, posters or messages. Ask yourself which meaning fits. In «cereal advertising», it is the business of adverts. In «The shop is advertising its new bikes», it is the action of telling people.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «The slogan that breakfast is "the most important meal" was spread partly by cereal advertising.» A slogan is a short, catchy phrase. Cereal advertising means the adverts for cereal that spread the slogan. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Advertising means making adverts to tell people about products or services and to persuade them to buy.
fact: Advertising is uncountable as a noun, so we say «more advertising», not «advertisings».
fact: «TV advertising» and «online advertising» are two common kinds of advertising.
fact: An «advertising campaign» is a planned series of adverts for one product, shown over a period of time.
fact: «False advertising» means adverts that make claims that are not true, and it is not allowed.
exercise: «Own-brand food costs less because there is no big advertising.» What does advertising mean here? | Teaching children to read | *Adverts that tell people about a product and persuade them to buy | A type of cheap packaging | Lessons about food
exercise: A company runs an «advertising campaign» for a new toy. What is a campaign? | A list of shops that sell toys | A toy that can fly | A short walk to the shop | *A planned series of adverts over a period of time
exercise: Which sentence uses advertising as the -ing form of «advertise»? | *The shop is advertising its new bikes on the radio | Cereal advertising is shown on Saturday morning | Online advertising costs a lot of money | False advertising is against the rules
test: Which of these are two common kinds of advertising? | Slogans and jokes | *TV advertising and online advertising | Toys and books | Breakfast and lunch
test: Why do companies use advertising? | To stop people buying anything | *To tell people about a product and persuade them to buy it | To make the product illegal | To show the weather forecast
exam: Which sentence uses «false advertising» correctly? | The advert was shown on a Tuesday | *An advert claims a drink gives you super powers, but it does not | The poster was bright and colourful | The advertising was on the bus
